gnment and termination part  of that plan  those problems were magnified by  specialist vanessa gian's murder  her body was found miles off base months  after she disappeared  we spoke exclusively to vanessa's sister  myra after this investigation was  commissioned this summer  do you feel like the soldiers on that  base are safe  i don't um it's one too many  either it's accidents or they claim to  be accidents  you know we don't really know the truth  different murders  outside inside the base and um  you know at this point i i don't feel  that  anyone is safe in there before her death  gehan told her family and friends she  had been sexually harassed  on base the army says it has no evidence  of an assault but an investigation into  her death is still ongoing  gehan's death launched a movement  worldwide thousands of former military  members shared their stories with the  hashtag i am vanessa guillen  that rally and cry also led to  legislative action  in september congress introduced the i  am vanessa guillen act  to change how the military handles  sexual assault within its ranks  but gian's family is not confident this  report  will provide them with any closure  natalie kawam is their attorney because  we can't ask  you know the wolf to guard the hen house  we can't ask them to  fix themselves we need to step up as  civilians  as the world together and do this for  them because  you know our military they're people too  and they need us  guam tells us the i am vanessa gui and  bill has stalled out in congress but  they are hoping to get a hearing for it  sometime  in the new year meanwhile contacts here  at the army tell us  they are already starting to implement  change and one of them is an overhaul  of the sexual assault and reporting  program here called  sharp more to come from fort hood later  today
 

